<title>ITALY: Italy's Trieste sees prelim Jan CPI at 0.1 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Italy's Trieste sees prelim Jan CPI at 0.1 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>TRIESTE, Italy 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Trieste said its January consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month-on-month and 2.6 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In December, Trieste's inflation rate was 0.2 percent and 2.8 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Trieste is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 2.49 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to December 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.1   (0.2)     2.6  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.3   (0.3)     3.2  (3.5)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0   (0.1)     3.4  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.6   (0.0)     4.2  (4.8)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0   (0.1)     3.3  (2.9)</p>
<p>    Health services		   1.6   (0.0)     2.3  (1.5)</p>
<p>    Transportation		   -0.6   (0.2)     2.7  (3.0)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -0.3   (0.2)     1.3  (3.2)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (0.0)     6.2  (6.2)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0   (0.0)     2.9  (3.9)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0   (0.0)    -0.8 (-0.7)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
